  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The turn – say hi and turn",
  "description": "Everyone has a ball and moves freely around the area. When you meet someone, you say hi to each other, then turn with the ball and go the other way. Try to say hi to as many as you can. Use the whole hall or mark a smaller area with cones.\n\nA turn is when you turn your body half a circle, with your chest and hips, and take the ball with you. Make it harder: turn with only one hand on the stick, or only towards your backhand side. Works well as a warm-up, or when there are new players in the team. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "How close can you get before the sticks clash?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Which way is easiest to turn? Why?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up after the turn – who do you say hi to next?"
    }
  ],
